  "reference": "Over-dispersion adjustment declining to engage. Twelve providers whose observed counts sit within Poisson noise of expected: the winsorized phi-hat = 0.022899 is below (K-1)/K, so Spiegelhalter 2005 eq. 10 sets tau-hat^2 = 0 and the limits are exactly the unadjusted exact Poisson oe limits (ucl[0] = interpolated Poisson(1.0030769 * 12) 0.999 quantile / 12 = 1.9709466). The adjustment never narrows below the null model. Cross-checked against an independent numpy + scipy.stats implementation of the whole chain (center line, Pearson residuals, winsorizing, method-of-moments tau^2, and the interpolated quantile of scipy's distribution) to ~1e-11.",
